mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course introduces the key aspects of research and development (R&D) for new drugs derived from traditional Chinese medicines (TCMs), including: (1) R&D strategy: focusing on the principles and methods of research topic selection; (2) Policies and regulations: interpreting registration categories for TCM new drugs and related policies and regulations; (3) Research content and methods: covering purification and formulation techniques, quality assessment, and pharmacological and toxicological evaluations; (4) Current status and evelopment: analyzing the landscape, challenges, and countermeasures for TCM new drugs. Additionally, the course integrates case studies of pharmacologists developing new drugs.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
